pment()` verifies separate GET confirms no change to order or shipment state\n   - Test `rejectIfOrderNotFound()` verifies 404 for unknown order\n   - Test `rejectShipmentCreationForCancelledOrder()` in ShipmentControllerTest verifies 409 when creating shipment for cancelled order\n\n6. **No new Maven dependency appears** ✓ — Only used existing Spring, Kotlin, JUnit dependencies\n\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** ✓ — Only modified:\n   - Order.kt: Added status field and OrderStatus enum (required)\n   - OrderRepository.kt: No changes needed (shipment lookup done in controller)\n   - OrderController.kt: Added cancel endpoint and injected ShipmentRepository\n   - ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId method (required for cancel logic)\n   - ShipmentController.kt: Added cancelled order validation (required)\n   - ApiError.kt: Added two new error codes (required)\n   - Tests: Added appropriate test cases\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **Order.kt**: Added `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field and OrderStatus enum. Necessary because requirement asks for order status field.\n\n- **OrderController.kt**: Injected ShipmentRepository and added `/cancel` endpoint. The endpoint checks order exists (404), handles idempotent repeat (200 if already cancelled), rejects if CONFIRMED shipment exists (409 with no state change), cancels CREATED shipments, persists order as CANCELLED. Necessary because requirement specifies this endpoint.\n\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Added `findByOrderId(orderId)` method. Necessary to retrieve all shipments for an order during cancellation.\n\n- **ShipmentController.kt**: Added order existence check and cancelled order validation before creating shipment. Necessary because requirement says \"creating a shipment for a cancelled order is rejected with HTTP 409\".\n\n- **ApiError.kt**: Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CREATED_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER error codes. Necessary to distinguish error cases.\n\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Added 6 new test cases covering all cancel scenarios. Necessary for verification.\n\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Added 1 new test case for cancelled order shipment rejection. Necessary for verification.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All cases named in the ticket are implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Customers may cancel an order until a carrier has accepted a shipment for it; add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel with ACTIVE/CANCELLED order statuses, idempotent cancellation, shipment cascade, and proper error handling.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added status field with OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) to track order lifecycle\n- OrderController.kt: Added POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint with all-or-nothing semantics and idempotency\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId method to support cancellation logic\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CREATED_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 6 tests for cancel endpoint covering success, persistence, cascading, idempotency, rejection cases\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for cancelled order shipment rejection\n\nTests:\n- `cancelsActiveOrder()` — POST cancel returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n- `verifyCancellationPersists()` — Separate GET confirms status persisted\n- `cancelsCREATEDShipments()` — CREATED shipments are transitioned to CANCELLED\n- `idempotentCancel()` — Repeat cancel on already-cancelled order succeeds\n- `rejectIfCONFIRMEDShipmentExists()` — Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409\n- `verifyNoStateChangeWhenCancelIsRejectedByCONFIRMEDShipment()` — Separate GET confirms order and shipment unchanged after rejection\n- `rejectIfOrderNotFound()` — Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n- `rejectShipmentCreationForCancelledOrder()` — Creating shipment for cancelled order returns 4